<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>SpeedTap Privacy Policy</title><style>body{margin:0;font:16px/1.65 system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,Arial,sans-serif;color:#18202b;background:#f4f6fb}main{max-width:820px;margin:36px auto;padding:32px;background:#fff;border-radius:16px;box-shadow:0 8px 32px #14234614}h1{line-height:1.2;color:#111827}h2{margin-top:28px;font-size:1.2rem}.notice{padding:12px 16px;background:#fff4d6;border-left:4px solid #d99a00;border-radius:6px}footer{margin-top:32px;color:#596579;font-size:.9rem}@media(max-width:600px){main{margin:0;padding:22px;border-radius:0}}</style></head><body><main>
<h1>SpeedTap Privacy Policy</h1><p><strong>Last updated:</strong> October 15, 2026</p>
<div class="notice"><strong>Before publishing:</strong> Replace the contact email placeholder below with a real email address you control, and verify that every section accurately describes the released app and its SDKs.</div>
<h2>1. Introduction</h2><p>This Privacy Policy explains how SpeedTap (“the App”) handles information when you use it.</p>
<h2>2. Information that may be processed</h2><p>Depending on the features enabled in the version you use, the App and its service providers may process:</p><ul><li><strong>Profile information:</strong> a username and account identifier, where profile features are used.</li><li><strong>Gameplay information:</strong> tap counts, completed rounds, personal bests, experience points, levels, combos, missions, and related progress.</li><li><strong>Diagnostics and usage information:</strong> information needed to operate, secure, and troubleshoot the App.</li><li><strong>Advertising information:</strong> advertising identifiers, device information, IP address, and ad interaction data may be processed by advertising providers, subject to the services and settings in use.</li></ul><p>The exact information processed depends on the features and third-party SDKs included in the published version.</p>
<h2>3. How information is used</h2><p>Information may be used to operate gameplay and profiles, save progress and records, provide leaderboards or missions where available, show and measure ads, prevent abuse, troubleshoot problems, improve reliability, and comply with legal obligations.</p>
<h2>4. Third-party services</h2><p>The App may use third-party services, including:</p><ul><li><strong>Google Firebase</strong> for app-related data storage and backend features, where enabled.</li><li><strong>Google AdMob</strong> for displaying and measuring advertisements and preventing advertising fraud, where enabled.</li></ul><p>These providers may process information under their own terms and privacy policies:</p><ul><li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a></li><li><a href="https://support.google.com/admob/">Google AdMob Help</a></li><li><a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy">Firebase Privacy and Security</a></li></ul>
<h2>5. Advertising</h2><p>The App may display personalized or non-personalized ads depending on availability, applicable requirements, consent choices, and device settings. You can manage some ad-related choices through your device settings and any consent options presented in the App. Limiting ad personalization does not necessarily stop ads from appearing.</p>
<h2>6. Storage and retention</h2><p>Information may be stored on your device or by cloud service providers, depending on the feature. Information is retained only as long as necessary for the purposes described here, unless a longer period is required or permitted by law. Retention periods can vary by data type and provider.</p>
<h2>7. Your choices and requests</h2><p>Depending on applicable law, you may have rights to request access to, correction of, or deletion of personal information, and to object to or restrict certain processing. Contact us using the email below to submit a request. Some information may need to be retained for legal, security, or operational reasons.</p>
<h2>8. Security</h2><p>Reasonable technical and organizational measures are used to protect information. No method of electronic storage or transmission can be guaranteed to be completely secure.</p>
<h2>9. Children's privacy</h2><p>The App is not intended to knowingly collect personal information from children in violation of applicable law. If you believe a child has provided personal information inappropriately, contact us so we can review the matter and take appropriate steps.</p>
<h2>10. International transfers</h2><p>Third-party providers may process or store information in countries outside your country of residence. Where required, applicable safeguards are used for such transfers.</p>
<h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2><p>This policy may be updated as the App, its service providers, or legal requirements change. The revised policy will be published on this page with an updated date.</p>
<h2>12. Contact</h2><p><strong>App:</strong> SpeedTap<br><strong>Contact email:</strong> <span style="color:#b45309">REPLACE-WITH-YOUR-REAL-CONTACT-EMAIL</span></p><footer>This policy should be reviewed against the actual data practices and SDK configuration of the published version of SpeedTap before use.</footer></main></body></html>
